# The Intech Grid (a PBF4 and an EN16, ui.c's map): their factory numbers on channel 1, the PBF4's keys mute, the
# EN16's pushes throw and reset, its Tracks layout, GLO's two pages, Learn, the map kept over a reboot
wait 300
expect pool 0x6AD
# off at first: a CC 36 is nobody's, a note 55 the scale's (the EN16's pushes are a keyboard's notes too)
midi B0 24 00
wait 20
expect par0 >0
# on: Song mode's KNOB 3 (GLO, GLO); then back to the Form page
tap GLO
wait 100
tap GLO
wait 100
expect view 28
spin K3 1
wait 1600
shot songmode.png
tap HOME
wait 100
expect view 0
# the PBF4, a column a track: fader F1 (CC 36) the chord's level, pot P1 (CC 32) the chord's track filter
midi B0 24 00
wait 20
expect par0 0
midi B0 24 7F
wait 20
expect par0 100
midi B0 20 00
wait 20
expect par148 -50
midi B0 20 40
wait 20
expect par148 0
# pot P4 (CC 35): the drums' filter, the kick's strip and the hats' both
midi B0 23 7F
wait 20
expect par156 50
expect par151 50
# another channel: not the Grid's
midi B1 24 00
wait 20
expect par0 100
# key B1 (note 40) mutes the chord, and again it's back; its notes don't touch the scale
midi 90 28 7F
wait 20
midi 90 28 00
wait 20
expect mutes 1
expect pool 0x6AD
midi 90 28 7F
wait 20
expect mutes 0
# key B4 (note 43): the drums, the kick and the hats both
midi 90 2B 7F
wait 20
expect mutes 24
midi 90 2B 7F
wait 20
expect mutes 0
# the EN16: encoder 1 (CC 48) the echo; its push (note 48) throws it while held
midi B0 30 19
wait 20
expect par8 20
midi 90 30 7F
wait 20
expect par8 100
midi 80 30 00
wait 20
expect par8 20
# encoder 2 (CC 49) the feedback; its push resets it to the piece's own
midi B0 31 00
wait 20
expect par11 0
midi 90 31 7F
wait 20
expect par11 >0
# GLO: Setup, Song mode, then the PBF4's page and the EN16's, then Setup again
tap GLO
wait 100
expect view 6
tap GLO
wait 100
expect view 28
tap GLO
wait 100
expect view 31
wait 1600
shot pbf4.png
tap GLO
wait 100
expect view 32
wait 1600
shot en16.png
# ALGORITHM on the EN16's page: Tracks. Encoder 1 the chord's track filter; encoder 4 the drums', the kick's and the
# hats' strips both
turn ALGO 1
wait 100
midi B0 30 00
wait 20
expect par148 -50
midi B0 33 7F
wait 20
expect par156 50
expect par151 50
# encoder 5's push (the echo sends' row, Throw): the chord's echo send up while held
midi B0 34 00
wait 20
expect par140 0
midi 90 34 7F
wait 20
expect par140 100
midi 90 34 00
wait 20
expect par140 0
wait 1600
shot tracks.png
turn ALGO 1
wait 100
# Learn on the PBF4's page: P1 chosen (KNOB 1), KNOB 3 to its left end, a CC binds it
tap GLO
wait 100
tap GLO
wait 100
tap GLO
wait 100
expect view 31
spin K3 -40
wait 1600
shot learn.png
# (the chord's filter -50 here, Tracks' encoder 1 left it so: the binding CC's own value doesn't move it)
midi B0 46 7F
wait 20
expect par148 -50
midi B0 46 40
wait 20
expect par148 0
midi B0 20 7F
wait 20
expect par148 0
# saved (GLO held), and kept over a reboot
press GLO
wait 700
release GLO
wait 100
expect dirty 0
reboot
wait 300
midi B0 46 7F
wait 20
expect par148 50
